# Citation metadata. GitHub renders this as the repository's "Cite this
# repository" button and generates BibTeX and APA from it; Zenodo reads it if
# this repository is ever archived there. `README.md` carries a hand-written
# BibTeX entry as well, because the generated one uses `@software`, which the
# older BibTeX styles do not know.
#
# There is no paper behind goatd, so this describes the software itself. If
# one is ever written, `preferred-citation` here redirects citations to it.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: goatd
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Van den Broeck
    given-names: Guy
    affiliation: University of California, Los Angeles
abstract: >-
  Greatest Of All Tree Decompositions: tree decompositions of graphs, as a Rust
  library and command-line solver. A portfolio runs greedy elimination orders,
  nested dissection and flow-based separation, and keeps the narrowest result.
keywords:
  - treewidth
  - tree decomposition
  - graph algorithms
  - elimination order
  - PACE
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/Tractables/goatd
url: https://tractables.github.io/goatd/
version: 0.1.2
date-released: '2026-08-30'
